@page
@model DevSecretStash.Api.Pages.IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Secure .NET Secrets Sync";
}

<section class="p-hero">
    <div class="wrap grid">
        <div>
            <p class="badge">Free &amp; open source</p>
            <h1>Dev Secret <span class="hot">Stash</span></h1>
            <p class="sub">Stop copying <strong>secrets.json</strong> between machines. Dev Secret Stash syncs your .NET user-secrets across every development machine with end-to-end encryption. The server never sees your plaintext.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
                <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/Register">Create free account <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
                <a class="btn btn-lg ghost" href="#features">See how it works</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="Terminal session: installing the dss tool, pushing secrets on one machine and pulling them on another">
            <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>dss</span></div>
<pre><span class="p">$</span> dotnet tool install --global DevSecretStash
<span class="p">$</span> dss register
<span class="ok">Registered and logged in</span>

<span class="p">$</span> dss push
<span class="ok">Pushed 5 keys</span> <span class="dim">(version: 1)</span>

<span class="dim"># On another machine:</span>
<span class="p">$</span> dss login
<span class="p">$</span> dss pull
<span class="ok">Pulled 5 keys</span> <span class="dim">(version: 1)</span><span class="cur"></span></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="marquee-track">
        <span>dss push</span><span>dss pull</span><span>AES-256-GCM</span><span>Argon2id</span><span>Zero knowledge</span><span>Self-hostable</span>
        <span>dss push</span><span>dss pull</span><span>AES-256-GCM</span><span>Argon2id</span><span>Zero knowledge</span><span>Self-hostable</span>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="sec-head reveal">
            <div>
                <span class="kicker">What it does</span>
                <h2>Your secrets,<br /><em>on every machine.</em></h2>
            </div>
            <p>Built for .NET developers. Everything you need to keep secrets in sync, and nothing you don't.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="features">
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">01</span><h3>End-to-end encrypted</h3><p>Secrets are encrypted on your machine with AES-256-GCM before they are uploaded.</p></div>
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">02</span><h3>Zero-knowledge server</h3><p>Your master key never leaves your machine. Even a compromised server can't read your secrets.</p></div>
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">03</span><h3>Two commands</h3><p><code>dss push</code> and <code>dss pull</code>. Your UserSecretsId is detected from the .csproj.</p></div>
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">04</span><h3>Works with dotnet user-secrets</h3><p>Same secrets.json format and the same file locations, so your existing workflow doesn't change.</p></div>
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">05</span><h3>Manage secrets directly</h3><p>The <code>dss secrets</code> commands create and edit collections without a project file.</p></div>
            <div class="feature reveal"><span class="ico">06</span><h3>Cross-platform</h3><p>Windows, macOS and Linux, reading and writing the standard user-secrets locations.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div class="reveal">
            <span class="kicker">Security model</span>
            <h2>The server only sees <em>ciphertext.</em></h2>
            <p class="body">A random master key encrypts your secrets. A key derived from your password with Argon2id wraps that master key, so changing your password never means re-encrypting everything.</p>
            <div class="shelf">
                <span class="ok">AES-256-GCM</span><span class="ok">Argon2id</span><span class="ok">HTTPS + HSTS</span><span class="ok">JWT + refresh tokens</span><span class="ok">Rate limiting</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
            <span class="kicker">Free, open and yours</span>
            <h2>Hosted here, or <em>self-host.</em></h2>
            <p class="body">Use the free hosted service at devsecretstash.com, or run your own instance on Azure App Service or Docker. The CLI points at whichever server you choose.</p>
            <div class="shelf">
                <span>.NET</span><span>dotnet global tool</span><span>ASP.NET Core</span><span>SQLite</span><span>Docker</span><span>MIT licence</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:30px">
                <a class="btn ghost" href="/Docs#deploy">Self-hosting guide <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
        <div class="reveal">
            <span class="kicker">Get started</span>
            <h2>Up and running in <em>60 seconds.</em></h2>
            <p class="body">Install the global tool, create an account, and push. Encryption keys are generated locally, and your password never leaves your machine in plaintext.</p>
            <a class="btn ghost" href="/Docs">Read the docs <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps reveal">
            <li><span class="n">01</span><div><h3>Install the CLI</h3><p><code>dotnet tool install --global DevSecretStash</code></p></div></li>
            <li><span class="n">02</span><div><h3>Create your account</h3><p>Run <code>dss register</code> or <a href="/Register">sign up here</a>.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="n">03</span><div><h3>Push your secrets</h3><p>From any .NET project, run <code>dss push</code>. Secrets are encrypted and uploaded.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="n">04</span><div><h3>Pull on another machine</h3><p><code>dss login</code>, then <code>dss pull</code>. Decrypted locally, written to the standard location.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section cta-big">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
        <span class="kicker">Free forever</span>
        <h2>Stop pasting secrets <span>into Slack.</span></h2>
        <p>No subscription, no limits, no credit card. Sync your first secrets in under a minute.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/Register">Create free account <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            <a class="btn btn-lg ghost" href="/Docs#install">Install the CLI</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
